Z||000000||BlackStang95||10-11-2001||12:47 PM||||How is the mod on fiero gt's with the clear decklid panel that shows the engine done?  it's the coolest one ive seen.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||10-11-2001||12:55 PM||||That would be Skitime.  I've seen it in person, and it looks even better in person!  He cut out the area in the deck lid using the bracing under the decklid as a guide.  Just made the hole as big as he could without cutting the bracing.  Then put a window in the opening.  That's the easy version.  I was more difficult than that, and I'm not sure what he used for the window, but the final result looks factory, and it's centered right over the plenum!  Awesome car.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||falconhulk||10-11-2001||01:12 PM||||Heh heh I thou je invented that until i saw the historic car races on speedvision last night!!!  There was a bunch of lambo's with this see through decklid window.......BTW Blackstang man , nice to see you have moved over to more constructive posts. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||10-11-2001||05:53 PM||||many exotic cars have glass panels in the decklid, but as far as I know, Skitime has the only Fiero one. (not including any of the Patriot kitcars..)<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
